1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,180
Operation NightFalcon critical security alert targeting OrionGate servers.

2
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:27,390
A critical zero-day vulnerability allows unauthenticated remote attackers to bypass access controls.

3
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:49,230
Designated CVE-2026-88421, remote code execution flaw in endpoint /api/v1/auth/gateway.

4
00:00:49,230 --> 00:01:08,910
Intrusion follows an eight-stage attack chain from initial access to command and control.

5
00:01:08,910 --> 00:01:25,250
Attributed to state-sponsored threat group Obsidian Kite, tracked as OK-17 and KiteGroup.

6
00:01:25,250 --> 00:02:01,150
Block C2 IPs 185.71.44.19, 91.203.18.77, 45.133.201.42, threat domains, and binary nfsvc.exe.

7
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:22,940
Intrusion timeline progression from September 4 scanning to September 8 emergency advisory.

8
00:02:22,940 --> 00:02:47,990
Enable detection across Network, Endpoint, DNS, and Web Logs.

9
00:02:47,990 --> 00:03:09,150
Execute mandatory response protocols: CONTAIN, INVESTIGATE, BLOCK, PATCH, and MONITOR.

10
00:03:09,150 --> 00:03:26,520
Critical threat: CVE-2026-88421 requires immediate action. Human review required before dissemination.
